  "id": "Compound::DB06204 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Tapentadol's relationship with Cyp2d6 is mediated through a shared pathway involving arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity. The evidence suggests that Tapentadol binds to Cyp2c19 and Cyp2c9, both of which participate in the metabolism of arachidonic acid, a key substrate for Cyp2d6. This implies that Tapentadol may influence Cyp2d6 through a mechanism involving the enzymatic activity of these cytochrome P450 enzymes. The lowest common ancestor of Tapentadol and Cyp2d6 is the organic cyclic compound, which is consistent with the involvement of these enzymes in metabolic processes. The presence of multiple pathways linking Tapentadol to Cyp2d6 highlights the complexity of its pharmacological interactions, with the arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity serving as a central node in the network. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of Cyp2d6 in the metabolic processing of arachidonic acid, potentially influenced by Tapentadol through its interaction with Cyp2c19 and Cyp2c9.",
